		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Repeater interface node as Hotspot?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5017&amp;p=36504#p36504"><![CDATA[
I've got a DMR repeater that isn't networked to Brandmeister (yet) and I'm not sure if I want to use the MMDVM/Pi Hat as the repeater controller without first asking if what my subject eludes to is possible.<br><br>I have an RT3S with OpenGD77 on it and while I know the radio is easily interfaced with the pi via USB to make a hot spot, is it possible to make that hot spot act like a traditional radio would to key a repeater? My guess is no, but I haven't tinkered around a whole lot due to time constraints. I would prefer to use the repeater's built-in controller and have a node radio be the interface.. <br><br>Another thought is to use the MMDVM/repeater interaface in simplex mode to work the basic functions but still keep the repeater working as I desire... but given the subscriber radio creates a handshake with the repeater, would an MMDVM in simplex be able to use the data to steer talkgroups and pass audio? <br><br>Anyone have insight or made either scenario work? <br><br>-Josh<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4051">W8JMO</a> — Fri Mar 28, 2025 6:52 pm</p><hr />
